   "default": "1",
   "doc": "On by default: each ring lane's data goes as a plain RDMA write and a 64-bit generation word is written after it to say it has arrived; the collecting kernel waits on those words. Set 0 for the flag-based arrival (the proxy publishes each lane's flag). The card's wait for the decode rings needs this on, with either arrival signal. Every node must agree.",
   "first_use": "families/dsv41/model.zig:1858",
   "default": "atomic",
   "doc": "How the generation word is sent: by default an RDMA atomic add, which the card executes only after the data writes are placed (the guaranteed arrival); word sends an 8-byte RDMA write instead. Every node must agree. A card without atomics: left unset, the rings send the write and say why in a warning; set to atomic, the start refuses by name.",
   "first_use": "families/dsv41/model.zig:1895",
