   ],
   "label": "Four-wide owner-sum add",
   "doc": "The owner sums' bf16 add (about 84 launches a 4,096-row pass, reading the transport's pages) runs four elements a thread with 16-byte loads. The same fp32 add and rounding, so the bytes are unchanged (replay: every output byte equal to the scalar kernel's in every page type); it cuts the time the add spends on the arena's locked pages. On unless 0.",
   "values": [],
   "seed": "name",
   "first_use": "families/dsv41/model.zig:2006",
   "secret": false
   "label": "Quality gate's canary (changes replies)",
   "doc": "Diagnostics for the quality gate only, never a serving setting: 1 the output head reads its rows after one more FP8 rounding step (the gate's ruler); 2 layer 0's MoE partials take one more FP8 step before their gather; 3 they move one fp32 ulp away from zero (a reduction order's size). A known small change the gate must detect; it changes replies. Every node must use the same setting (a start whose nodes differ is refused). Leave unset.",
  },
