   "label": "Router GEMM on a 64-row tile",
   "doc": "The router's bf16 GEMM of a prompt chunk (384 experts, K 5,120; the owned rows) runs on a 64 x 64 tile of 128 threads, two blocks an SM, instead of the 128 x 128 tile of 256 threads: at a 4,096-row pass's 1,024 owned rows its grid is 24 blocks on 48 SMs, half the GPU idle, and 96 on the smaller tile. A warp's MMA chain and every output element's K chain are the same (no split-K), so the bytes are the 128 x 128 tile's (kernels replay pf_t64); each rank decides for itself. Off until the kernel time is measured on the Spark.",
